            563
          ]
        }
      ],
      "orig": "Each time a unit shoots, before any attacks are resolved, you must select the enemy units that will be the targets for all of the ranged weapons you wish its models to make attacks with. Each time you select a target for a model's ranged weapon, you can only select an enemy unit as the target if at least one model in that unit is both within range of that weapon and visible to that attacking model (pg 8). An enemy model is within range of a weapon if the distance between it and the attacking model is equal to or less than that weapon's Range characteristic.",
      "text": "Each time a unit shoots, before any attacks are resolved, you must select the enemy units that will be the targets for all of the ranged weapons you wish its models to make attacks with. Each time you select a target for a model's ranged weapon, you can only select an enemy unit as the target if at least one model in that unit is both within range of that weapon and visible to that attacking model (pg 8). An enemy model is within range of a weapon if the distance between it and the attacking model is equal to or less than that weapon's Range characteristic."
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/460",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/body"
      },
      "children": [],
      "content_layer": "body",
      "label": "text",
      "prov": [
        {
          "page_no": 19,
          "bbox": {
            "l": 306.1417,
